                  <strong>Weeks-not-years falsifiability:</strong> hypotheses must be refutable by
                  clean ablations (e.g., knocking out counting vs. sorting circuits).
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>Inspectable mechanistic artifact:</strong> every study must yield a
                  concrete taxonomy, ablation matrix, or deployable routing table—not just an
                  efficiency curve.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>Real-world benchmark validity:</strong> evaluated across 4K long-context
                  tasks (RULER, LongBench-Qasper), Python synthesis, and HumanEval rather than
                  isolated toy circuits.
                </li>
